/-!
# Actual natural and augmentation-core extensions in the S₈ source branch

The cochain calculations use the seven adjacent transpositions in the
literal eight-letter action. Lean's kernel checks each finite mask identity.
A natural self-extension has one possible parity class beyond coboundaries;
that class moves at least six dimensions under a transposition, so the
source rank-two condition excludes it. An augmentation-core-by-natural
extension has no remaining class. Correcting a chosen quotient section
therefore constructs invariant complements to the specified kernels.

The public marked conclusions retain the original actor identification and
give either the whole natural-pair equivalence or an equivariant surjection
onto the augmentation core. These are the outputs used by the fixed cyclic
seed obstruction in original 14.7.51; no splitting premise is supplied.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 14.7.51, printed p.1065, refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/
